<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.15;" data-page-h1>
          AI drafts for posts and ads, with approvals, for an events marketing team
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-0" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 980px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);">
          We modernized a legacy events platform to a React based UI and built an AI driven marketing workflow: generate posts + ad creative, schedule to Meta (Facebook/Instagram), generate campaigns
          for Meta and Google, and enforce governance with guardrails and explainable &ldquo;why this copy/targeting&rdquo; reports.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The problem</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            Event operators run a tight loop: announce, build momentum, convert, and keep audiences warm until doors open. For teams managing dozens of events,
            marketing execution becomes repetitive, manual, and error prone, especially when content, creative, and ad setup must be rebuilt for every venue and date.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            Billy Martin needed Vesta (EventVesta.com) to support a modern, scalable marketing flow: fast content production, multi channel scheduling, performance safe AI automation,
            and a calendar based workflow that keeps promoters on track.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <%= render "home/case_studies/at_a_glance",
            industry: "Events / marketing",
            client: "EventVesta (Vesta)",
            country: "[[AHMAD: country]]",
            what_we_built: "React UI modernization plus AI marketing OS for posts, ads, and scheduling",
            integrations: "Meta Graph API (Facebook/Instagram), Google Ads API, media storage/CDN",
            stack: "React (UI), API services, Postgres, background workers" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="what-we-built">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we built</h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          We rebuilt the front end experience with React and then designed an &ldquo;AI marketing OS&rdquo; around Vesta&rsquo;s event data. The system ingests event details (artist/lineup, venue, timing, ticket
          tiers, audience segments) and creative inputs (images, brand voice, past performance signals) to generate campaign ready assets.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          The result is a robust workflow: content and ad generation, scheduling, approvals, and a centralized calendar that orchestrates the marketing timeline for each event, from announcement
          through last call reminders.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How it works</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-4" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>AI content generation with context:</strong> Event metadata + brand voice + creative constraints produce posts and ad copy that stay on message.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi channel scheduling:</strong> Automated scheduling to Facebook + Instagram, with a calendar view and publishing guardrails.</li>
          <li><strong>Ad generation with explainability:</strong> Meta + Google campaign drafts include an AI analysis report describing why specific audiences, budgets, and angles were chosen.</li>
          <li><strong>Safety &amp; governance:</strong> Hard rules, approvals, audit logs, and &ldquo;do not publish&rdquo; switches prevent unsafe or off brand automation.</li>
          <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> React (UI) &rarr; API services &rarr; Postgres + background workers for generation/scheduling.</li>
          <li><strong>AI features:</strong> Post + ad copy generation, image analysis, event summarization, and campaign rationale reports.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/demo_walkthrough", youtube_id: "jeRFBiBu_-g", iframe_title: "Vesta event management platform demo" %>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Results</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-0" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Faster marketing cycles:</strong> generate post calendars, ad drafts, and creative variations in minutes instead of days.</li>
          <li><strong>Consistent execution:</strong> repeatable, calendar driven workflows across many concurrent events.</li>
          <li><strong>Higher confidence automation:</strong> explainable AI reports and approval controls reduce risk while scaling output.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/gallery", slug: "eventvesta-ai-marketing" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/client_quote", slug: "eventvesta-ai-marketing" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/cta", blurb: "We&rsquo;ll design the workflow, guardrails, and integrations, then ship in phases so you can scale output without losing control." %>

  <section class="py-4 bg-white">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <%= link_to "B2B SaaS →", industry_b2b_saas_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>